    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "In this code supplement to the paper \"Optimal Shrinkage of Singular Values\" we offer a Matlab software library that includes:\r\n\r\n- A function that optimally shrinks singular values, for Frobenius, Operator, or Nuclear norm losses, in known or unknown noise level. \r\n- Scripts that generate each of the figures in this paper. \r\n- Note that the scripts that generates Figures 4 and 5 shows how to numerically compute optimal shrinkers where a closed-form solution is unavailable.",
